This package was originally used to read the spherical-harmonic coefficients at a given depth 
stored in the DSM output files and then compute time-domain Green’s functions at specified 
epicentral distances. The current SEM–DSM coupling scheme no longer requires this intermediate 
step, because the Green’s functions at the target distances are computed directly during 
the DSM stage. This modification simplifies the already complex SEM–DSM coupling workflow by
reducing the number of processing steps. The tradeoff, however, is reduced computational 
efficiency, since the calculations of spherical-harmonic coefficients and distance-dependent 
Green’s functions are now combined into a single stage rather than treated separately.
